.TH INKWELL 1 "" "Inkwell" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
inkwell \- collaborative Typst and Markdown editor, without a server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B inkwell
.RI [ FILE | FOLDER ]...
.br
.B inkwell
.B \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Inkwell
opens a window to write Typst or Markdown documents, alone or with other people.
People who write together are connected directly to each other; there is no account
and no server. Each person keeps a full copy of the project on their computer, edits
continue offline, and they are merged when people meet again.
.PP
Without an argument, Inkwell opens the most recent project of the Inkwell folder in the
Documents folder of the user, and creates one on first launch. Given a
.I FILE
or a
.I FOLDER
of a project of that folder, it opens that project and shows the file.
.PP
Only one Inkwell runs per profile
.RB ( INKWELL_HOME ).
When it is already running, a new
.B inkwell
hands its arguments and its working directory to it and exits: the running window comes
to the front and shows the file. A file it cannot show yet is named in a message of that
window. If the running Inkwell does not answer within 5 seconds, a notification says so
and the new one exits with status 3; if the profile folder cannot be locked, Inkwell does
not start and exits with status 4.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version (SemVer), the commit and the build date, then exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B INKWELL_DOCS
Folder that holds the projects, instead of
.IR Inkwell " in the Documents folder."
.TP
.B INKWELL_HOME
Folder that holds the identity of the user (the keys), instead of
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/inkwell .
.TP
.B INKWELL_LAN
Set to
.B 1
to find other people on the local network.
.TP
.B INKWELL_RENDEZVOUS
URL of the server that carries the short invitation codes; the word
.B off
turns the codes off.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/Documents/Inkwell/
The projects. Their files are ordinary files; uninstalling Inkwell never touches them.
.TP
.I ~/.config/inkwell/
The identity of the user.
.SH SEE ALSO
Typst, https://typst.app/docs/
.PP
Project home page, https://github.com/oioio-space/inkwell
